{
  "description": "#5140 Phase 4a — `apply_page_source` saves a page edited as its source buffer: the buffer is diffed against the page's own render by `^ID` anchor, and the difference is written as edits, moves, creates and deletes. Covers only what the tauri mock models, so every seeded block is plain single-line text (no task markers, list styles, properties or names, and no `[[`, `#`, `->` or `::`), which both stacks' `get_page_source` render byte for byte as `- content ^ID`; the anchors are the seed labels' expanded ids. Each successful step's `baseSource` is the page's source after the step before it, so every step also passes the stale check; the create runs last because its block's id is minted per stack. One kind of change per step, so the op log's order does not depend on the order the command writes kinds in, and the delete is kept out of a reordered sibling group. Seed: S1 (Home) > S2 (alpha), S3 (bravo), S4 (charlie), S5 (delta) > S6 (echo); S7 (Elsewhere) > S8 (foreign). Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
